export default "import { Meta } from '@storybook/addon-docs/blocks';\n\n<Meta title=\"Documentation/Current State - What's Actually Built\" />\n\n# Current State: What's ACTUALLY Built vs Planned\n\n## ✅ What ACTUALLY Works Right Now\n\n### Database Persistence\n- **PostgreSQL CRUD** - Sessions save and load properly\n- **Field names fixed** - snake_case conversion works\n- **Content persists** - All three columns save to database\n\n### Three-Column Workspace\n- **Left Column** - Prompt builder with sections (works)\n- **Middle Column** - Shows raw output after RUN (works)\n- **Right Column** - Grace AI chat interface (works)\n\n### Editors Available (Manual Trigger Only)\n- **Lexical Editor** - Can be manually loaded via event\n- **Markdown Editor** - Can be manually loaded via event\n- **NOT automatic** - Must be triggered explicitly\n\n### Event System\n- Cross-column communication works\n- Grace can trigger events with XML commands\n- Manual event dispatch works\n\n### LIT Components\n- `<status-indicator>` - Registered and works\n- `<project-card-element>` - Registered and works\n- Can be rendered when AI emits XML tags\n\n## ❌ What's NOT Built (But Documented As If It Is)\n\n### Intelligent Output Selection\n**Claimed:** AI automatically chooses which editor to load based on prompt\n**Reality:** Always shows raw text output - no intelligent routing\n\n### Tool Call Processing\n**Claimed:** Tool Call section determines output type\n**Reality:** Tool Call content is sent to AI but doesn't affect output display\n\n### Context Inference\n**Claimed:** AI infers from \"write\" → Lexical, \"documentation\" → Markdown\n**Reality:** No inference logic implemented\n\n### Automatic Editor Loading\n**Claimed:** Editors load automatically after RUN\n**Reality:** Only raw text appears - editors need manual trigger\n\n## 🔧 How Things ACTUALLY Work\n\n### When You Hit RUN:\n1. Prompt sections collected and sent to backend\n2. AI processes and returns text/markdown\n3. Text appears in middle column textarea\n4. That's it - no smart routing\n\n### To Load Lexical Editor:\n```javascript\n// Must manually dispatch this event\nwindow.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('inject-content', {\n  detail: { type: 'lexical-editor', content: 'text' }\n}));\n```\n\n### To Load Markdown Editor:\n```javascript\n// Must manually dispatch this event\nwindow.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('inject-content', {\n  detail: { type: 'markdown-editor', content: 'text' }\n}));\n```\n\n## 🌐 Production Setup: Ngrok Tunnel\n\n### What It Is\n- **Ngrok** (not Cloudflare) creates a tunnel from your local backend to the internet\n- Your local backend (port 5001) becomes accessible via public URL\n- Production site at `https://prompt-portal-prod.raibach.net` uses this tunnel\n\n### How It Works\n```\nLocal Backend (5001) → Ngrok Tunnel → Public URL → Production Site\n```\n\n### Setup Commands\n```bash\n# Start the tunnel\n./keep_tunnel_running.sh\n\n# This will:\n# 1. Kill existing ngrok processes\n# 2. Start new tunnel on port 5001\n# 3. Update proxy.php with new URL\n# 4. Show the public URL\n```\n\n### Why This Matters\n- Allows testing production frontend with local backend\n- No need to deploy backend for every change\n- Real-time testing with production environment\n\n## 📊 Honest Assessment\n\n### Working Well ✅\n- Database persistence\n- Basic three-column layout\n- Event system\n- Component infrastructure\n\n### Needs Implementation ❌\n- Intelligent tool selection\n- Automatic editor loading\n- Tool Call processing\n- Context inference\n\n### Architecture Present ✅\n- All editors exist and work\n- Event system can trigger them\n- Frontend can render them\n- Just missing the \"brain\" to choose\n\n## For Developers: Next Steps\n\n### To Implement Smart Output Selection:\n1. **Backend**: Add logic to `grace_gui.py`:\n```python\ndef determine_output_type(prompt_data):\n    tool_call = prompt_data.get('Tool Call', '')\n    if 'lexical-editor' in tool_call:\n        return {'type': 'lexical-editor'}\n    # etc...\n```\n\n2. **Frontend**: Update `PromptWorkspace.tsx`:\n```typescript\n// After getting response\nif (response.outputType === 'lexical-editor') {\n  window.dispatchEvent(new CustomEvent('inject-content', {\n    detail: { type: 'lexical-editor', content: response.output }\n  }));\n}\n```\n\n### Current Workaround:\nGrace can manually load editors with:\n```xml\n<load_tool name=\"lexical-editor\"/>\n```\n\n## Bottom Line\n\n**What's Real:**\n- Database works ✅\n- Editors exist ✅\n- Can be manually triggered ✅\n\n**What's Missing:**\n- Automatic selection ❌\n- Smart routing ❌\n- Tool Call processing ❌\n\nThe infrastructure is there, but the intelligence isn't connected yet."